"""
Astrowatch -- birth-chart corpus for famous people across multiple fields, built at
explicit user request to extend the leadership pattern-mining work to a much larger,
cross-field population (actors, musicians, athletes, scientists, business leaders,
authors, artists/directors).

DATA HONESTY (identical convention to leaders_corpus.py / events_corpus.py):
- Birth DATES are drawn from general, well-established public biographical knowledge
  (the same standard used throughout this project for historical events/leaders) --
  not individually re-verified live for all ~1000 entries this pass. A small number
  were spot-checked live this session (2025 Nobel laureates, 2026 Oscar winners) to
  avoid stale-knowledge errors on very recent honorees.
- Birth TIMES: the small subset with a specific, credibly-documented time (mostly
  from long-standing astrological reference databases with birth-certificate-level
  sourcing, e.g. Astro-Databank "Rodden Rating" AA/A entries commonly cited for
  Hollywood/music-industry figures) are tagged time_source='DOCUMENTED'. Everyone
  else uses ASSUMED_NOON local time, per this session's standing instruction --
  which is the overwhelming majority of entries here. Ascendant/house placements
  for ASSUMED_NOON entries are NOT reliable; Moon Rasi/Nakshatra and Mahadasha lord
  are comparatively more usable (low time-sensitivity).
- LOCATION: birthplace city-level coordinates.
"""

PEOPLE = []

def _add(name, date, time, tz, country, lat, lon, field, note):
    PEOPLE.append((name, date, time, tz, country, lat, lon, field, note))

